at the beginning of our presidency  indeed before our presidency we had  announced that two of our major  priorities were the issue of childhood  obesity and the issue of cross-border  cooperation with health systems today we  have to say that we have adopted council  conclusions on both priorities obesity  is a European challenge and must be  addressed not just by health ministers  and the health council but across the  whole of the European Union and its  institutions the second conclusions  conclusions that were adopted today  regarded reven voluntary cross-border  cooperation and again this is a very  important concept and I think there is  much scope for for collaboration between  member states especially on a voluntary  basis in the coming months and years the  provision of health services is member  state competence and must remain as such  however having said that there is a  large scope for collaboration between  institutions and and and member states  across the European Union the third item  that we discussed today was the health  aspect on the applications to health  generated by the European pillar of  social rights I'm particularly glad we  had an opportunity to discuss health  aspects of European pillar of social  rights looking at the health principle I  would like to highlight that timely  access means everyone should be able to  access health care whenever they need it  affordable health care means people  should not be prevented from getting the  care they need because of the course  health care good quality means that  health care should be relevant  appropriate safe and effective
 

